"Community-Statement-on-completion-of-PrProfile-Regimen-3-enrollment-AU-FINAL-091826.pdf (https://www.cjdsupport.org.au/?pdfemb-)\nciteturn93search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; stage (Phase 1/2) clinical trial designed to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics, and ... March 2026: Ionis expanded PrProfile to explore an additional dosing regimen (known as ... an encouraging safety and tolerability profile and that ION717 is engaging with its target\nSeptember 2026\nDear Prion Disease Community,\nIonis is pleased to inform you that we have completed enrollment of Regimen 3 of PrProfile, an early-\nstage (Phase 1/2) clinical trial designed to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics, and\npharmacodynamics of ION717 in people with symptomatic prion disease.1\nPrProfile Clinical Development Timeline\nDecember 2023: Ionis initiated PrProfile, enrolling people with symptomatic prion\ndisease into Regimen 1 and Regimen 2. P articipants in Regimens 1 and 2 received\nmultiple injections of study drug (ION717 and placebo) during a 30-week double-blind\nT reatment P eriod during which the order of injections (i.e., ION717 or placebo) was\nblinded. Individuals who complete the double-blind Treatment Period were eligible to\ntransition to an open-label e xtension (OLE) Treatment Period.1\nDecember 2024: Ionis complet ed enrollment of Regimens 1 & 2.2\nMarch 2026: Ionis expanded PrProfile to explore an additional dosing regimen (known as\nRegimen 3) and extend the OLE for participants enrolled in Regimen 1 & 2. The decision\nto implement these changes was based on a pre-planned review of interim data showing\nan encouraging safety and tolerability profile and that ION717 is engaging with its target\nbiology (i.e., prion protein). Unlike earlier regimens, Regimen 3 is open-label, meaning\nthere is no placebo received during the Treatment Period – only ION717.3\nAugust 2026: Ionis completed enrollment of Regimen 3. PrProfile remains ongoing, with\nparticipants from across all Regimens continuing to receive doses of ION717 and\ncomplete assessments per the study protocol.1\nIonis thanks all PrProfile participants, their caregivers, and site investigators and staff for their\ntremendous collaboration and efforts in helping advance this research. We also wish to express our\ngratitude to the global prion disease community for your support throughout this program and look\nforward to providing updates in the future.\nSincerely,\nThe ION717 Team\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrProfile: A Study to Assess the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of ION717 | Clinical Research Trial Listing (https://www.centerwatch.com/clinical-trials/listings/NCT06153966/prprofile-a-study-to-assess-the-safety-tolerability-pharmacokinetics-and-pharmacodynamics-of-ion717)\nciteturn93search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Last updated: September 15, 2026 ... The purpose of this study is to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of intrathecal (IT) delivery of ION717. ...   * Patients must have a caregiver who is ≥ 18 years old and who is able and willing to facilitate the patient's involvement, to the best of their ability, for the duration of the trial; caregivers must also be able and willing to provide information about themselves and the patient for the duration of the trial.\n\n# PrProfile: A Study to Assess the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of ION717\n\nLast updated: September 15, 2026\n\nSponsor: Ionis Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\n\nOverall Status: Active - Not Recruiting\n\n#### Phase\n\n1/2\n\n#### Condition\n\nN/A\n\n#### Treatment\n\nPlacebo\n\nION717\n\n#### Clinical Study ID\n\nNCT06153966\n\nION717-CS2\n\n2023\n\n2023-503355-98\n\n  * Ages > 18\n  * All Genders\n\n### Study Summary\n\nThe purpose of this study is to evaluate the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of intrathecal (IT) delivery of ION717.\n\n## Eligibility Criteria\n\n#### Inclusion\n\nKey Inclusion Criteria\n\n  * A confirmed diagnosis of probable or definite prion disease.\n\n  * Early-stage prion disease at the time of Screening.\n\n  * Willing to meet all study requirements, including travel to Study Center, procedures, measurements and visits.\n\n  * Patients must have a caregiver who is ≥ 18 years old and who is able and willing to facilitate the patient's involvement, to the best of their ability, for the duration of the trial; caregivers must also be able and willing to provide information about themselves and the patient for the duration of the trial.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nION717 Phase 1/2 — 13 sites, updated Sep 2026 | DataLookout (https://dashboard.datalookout.com/trial/NCT06153966)\nciteturn93search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; # PrProfile: A Study to Assess the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of ION717 ... Mar 13, 2026 Trial status: Active, Not Recruiting to Recruiting v21 Show 6 more changes Show less\n\nNCT06153966\n\n# PrProfile: A Study to Assess the Safety, Tolerability, Pharmacokinetics and Pharmacodynamics of ION717\n\nStatus Active, Not Recruiting\n\nPhase Phase 1/2\n\nSponsorIonis Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\n\nPrimary completion Apr 2027 (estimated)\n\nAt risk: Primary completion moved at least 32 days later.\n\n## Record History\n\nAll 34 versions: 30 with changes below, 4 re-verified with no change. See every version on ClinicalTrials.gov ↗\n\n  1. Sep 15, 2026 Primary completion pushed from Feb 2027 to Apr 2027\n     * Study completion pushed from Jun 2030 to Aug 2030\n     * Study description shortened, about 7 words\n\n  2. Sep 11, 2026 Eligibility criteria expanded, about 10 words\n     * Primary completion date: Feb 2027 to Apr 2027\n     * Study completion date: Jun 2030 to Aug 2030\n     * Secondar